<title>USA: U.S. propane stocks fall 2.3 mln barrels in week.</title>
<headline>U.S. propane stocks fall 2.3 mln barrels in week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. inventories of propane drew 2.3 million barrels in the week to about 40 million barrels, falling in all major areas of the country, showed the latest Energy Information Administration report on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In the week ending Jan. 10, the Gulf Coast drew 1.6 million barrels to 21.1 million, which is within the normal range for this time of year, said the EIA.</p>
<p>The Midwest fell 500,000 barrels to 12.6 million, which is below normal range, and the East Coast edged down about 500,000 to 4.41 million -- above normal range, the EIA said.</p>
